  "test": {
    "name": "SafeNet KZ blind held-out test set v1",
    "provenance": {
      "type": "synthetic",
      "author": "independent agent without access to detector rules",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-25",
      "labelPolicy": "expectedRisk=true means a human analyst SHOULD review the item because it promotes or organizes one of the three schemes (offer, invitation, recruitment, native promotion); category = track (lottery: paid participation in a draw with random winner selection and organizer income; casino: direct or hidden online-casino promotion via referral/tracking links, promo codes, mirrors, shorteners, proxy channels, native 'my win' content, streams, emoji/leetspeak masking; pyramid: investment demands with unrealistic/guaranteed returns, urgency, referral rewards, payout 'proof', curator structure). expectedRisk=false with category 'none' covers everything else: free contests (subscribe/like/repost, no payment); legal ads (bank deposits ~14-17%/year, store discount promo codes, licensed state lottery news); news, police/agency reports and awareness posts that describe or quote schemes in order to warn; charity fundraising to a card for a named cause without promised returns; ordinary video-game streams without gambling links; job ads; financial-literacy education; draws among buyers of a normal product at no extra charge. Paying specifically for a ticket/number/slot/entry to a draw is lottery risk even if the prize is small, including when framed as charity or as a worthless 'product'. Genuinely ambiguous items were excluded.",
      "limitations": "Fully synthetic texts written by a single LLM author; labels were assigned by that same author with no second annotator and no inter-annotator agreement measured. The author did not see the detector, but shares general knowledge of scheme vocabulary with whoever wrote the rules, so lexical overlap is plausible and real-world performance may be lower. Class balance (165 positive / 165 negative) is artificial; real feeds have far lower prevalence, so precision on live data will be lower than on this set. Kazakh, code-mixed and transliterated texts are not native-speaker verified and may contain unnatural phrasing; real slang evolves quickly. Screenshots, images and streams are represented only as idealized OCR/transcript text (no OCR noise model, no audio errors). Hard negatives were deliberately constructed to share surface words with scams, so the false-positive rate here is a stress test, not an estimate of production FPR. All brands, people, phone numbers, cards and domains are fictional placeholders (.example domains, +7 700 000 XX XX numbers, masked cards), which may make some cues easier or harder than in real data. Small per-cell counts (e.g. per language x category) give wide confidence intervals."
    },
